      "text": [
        "2252 - وَ رُوِيَ : «أَنَّ اَلْحَاجَّ وَ اَلْمُعْتَمِرَ يَرْجِعَانِ كَمَوْلُودَيْنِ مَاتَ أَحَدُهُمَا طِفْلاً لاَ ذَنْبَ لَهُ وَ عَاشَ اَلْآخَرُ مَا عَاشَ مَعْصُوماً »."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.2252 - It has been narrated: \"The pilgrim and the one performing Umrah return like two newborns—one who died as an infant without sin, and the other who lived their life free from sin.\""
        ]
      }
